// Editor-only configuration. The enforced gates stay mypy (app, engine,
// evaluations, mcp_server) and ruff; nothing in CI reads this file. It exists
// because an editor's Pyright, rooted at the repo, resolves neither the
// interpreter nor the import roots: it has no venv to read third-party
// packages from, so every third-party import in a file that is perfectly
// type-clean under mypy reads as an unknown symbol.
//
// One venv per config is all Pyright supports, so this points at the root
// .venv that the Makefile builds (VENV := $(ROOT)/.venv) and that every test
// target runs from -- it carries the editable co_scientist_engine install.
// It deliberately does *not* point at app/.venv,
// which is a stale leftover missing declared dependencies (pypdf) and produces phantom unresolved-import errors. The
// mcp_server package keeps its own 3.12 environment at .venv-mcp (see
// AGENTS.md) whose third-party imports this cannot resolve; run mypy from
// engine/mcp_server for that package.
//
// executionEnvironments is first-match-wins, so engine/mcp_server must stay
// ahead of engine. The evaluations entry carries "." because its modules
// import themselves by their package path ("from evaluations._artifacts import
// ...") , which needs the repository root on the path, not the package dir.
//
// reportUnusedFunction is off because it is structurally wrong for this
// codebase, not merely noisy. Pyright treats a leading underscore as "private
// to this module" and does no reverse-dependency search, but this repo's
// split convention deliberately moves _private helpers into sibling modules
// that the parent re-exports, so the seams tests monkeypatch keep resolving.
// Measured over app + engine + evaluations: 315 functions flagged, of which
// 311 are referenced from another file and 3 more are FastAPI route handlers
// reached through their @app.get decorator. One was genuinely dead. At that
// ratio the rule generates delete-lists that would remove working code. The
// cost of switching it off is that a dead private function no longer
// announces itself; grep-tracing a suspect symbol repo-wide is the
// replacement, and is what found the one real case.
{
  "venvPath": ".",
  "venv": ".venv",
  "pythonVersion": "3.12",
  "reportUnusedFunction": "none",
  "exclude": [
    "**/node_modules",
    "**/__pycache__",
    "**/.venv*",
    "**/build",
    "**/dist",
    "references",
    "corpus"
  ],
  "executionEnvironments": [
    {
      "root": "app",
      "extraPaths": ["engine/src"]
    },
    {
      "root": "engine/mcp_server",
      "extraPaths": ["engine"]
    },
    {
      "root": "engine",
      "extraPaths": ["engine/src"]
    },
    {
      "root": "evaluations",
      "extraPaths": [".", "evaluations", "app", "engine/src"]
    }
  ]
}
